            "bug_id": 19051,
            "text": "Created attachment 3673\nAdd and use a helper for safe truncation / downcasting.\n\nThere are a number of locations where R downcasts values without checking if the casted value would fit the target type. For example (using a version of R built with ASAN + UBSAN)\n\n```\n> 1[1e101]\nsubset.c:716:10: runtime error: 1e+101 is outside the range of representable values of type 'long'\nSUMMARY: UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer: undefined-behavior subset.c:716:10\nsubscript.c:803:28: runtime error: 1e+101 is outside the range of representable values of type 'long'\nSUMMARY: UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer: undefined-behavior subscript.c:803:28\nsubscript.c:843:27: runtime error: 1e+101 is outside the range of representable values of type 'long'\nSUMMARY: UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer: undefined-behavior subscript.c:843:27\nsubscript.c:861:24: runtime error: 1e+101 is outside the range of representable values of type 'long'\nSUMMARY: UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer: undefined-behavior subscript.c:861:24\nsubset.c:145:2: runtime error: 1e+101 is outside the range of representable values of type 'long'\nSUMMARY: UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer: undefined-behavior subset.c:145:2\n[1] NA\n> R.version\n               _\nplatform       x86_64-pc-linux-gnu\narch           x86_64\nos             linux-gnu\nsystem         x86_64, linux-gnu\nstatus         Under development (unstable)\nmajor          4\nminor          7.0\nyear           2026\nmonth          04\nday            13\nsvn rev        89874\nlanguage       R\nversion.string R Under development (unstable) (2026-04-13 r89874)\nnickname       Unsuffered Consequences\n```\n\nThese are mostly triggered via unnaturally large index vectors (and so shouldn't occur in practice, at least not intentionally) but figured I would file for completeness. That said, it's not clear what the correct behavior in each scenario is -- e.g. emit an R error, versus silent truncation.\n\n\n      216 +| # | File | Line(s) | Cast |\n      217 +|---|---|---|---|\n      218 +| 1 | `src/main/subset.c` | 86 | `(R_xlen_t) (di - 1)` |\n      219 +| 2 | `src/main/subset.c` | 716 | `(R_xlen_t) rval` |\n      220 +| 3 | `src/main/subscript.c` | 136 | `(R_xlen_t)(dblind - 1)` |\n      221 +| 4 | `src/main/subscript.c` | 254 | `(R_xlen_t)(dblind - 1)` |\n      222 +| 5 | `src/main/subscript.c` | 803 | `(R_xlen_t) max` |\n      223 +| 6 | `src/main/subscript.c` | 805 | `(R_xlen_t) max` |\n      224 +| 7 | `src/main/subscript.c` | 840 | `(R_xlen_t) ds` |\n      225 +| 8 | `src/main/subscript.c` | 843 | `(R_xlen_t) ds` |\n      226 +| 9 | `src/main/subscript.c` | 861 | `(R_xlen_t) ds` |\n      227 +| 10 | `src/main/mapply.c` | 52 | `(R_xlen_t) REAL(ans)[0]` |\n      228 +| 11 | `src/main/summary.c` | 1181 | `(R_xlen_t)REAL(ans)[i] - 1` |\n      229 +| 12 | `src/main/altclasses.c` | 53 | `(R_xlen_t) REAL0(info)[0]` |\n      230 +| 13 | `src/main/altclasses.c` | 55 | `(int) REAL0(info)[1]` |\n      231 +| 14 | `src/main/altclasses.c` | 57 | `(int) REAL0(info)[2]` |\n      232 +| 15 | `src/main/altclasses.c` | 60 | `(R_xlen_t) REAL0(info)[0]` |\n      233 +| 16 | `src/main/altclasses.c` | 61 | `(int) REAL0(info)[1]` |\n      234 +| 17 | `src/main/altclasses.c` | 62 | `(int) REAL0(info)[2]` |\n      235 +| 18 | `src/main/altclasses.c` | 359 | `(R_xlen_t) REAL0(info)[0]` |\n      236 +| 19 | `src/main/altclasses.c` | 402 | `(R_xlen_t) REAL_ELT(x, 0)` |\n      237 +| 20 | `src/library/stats/src/splines.c` | 447 | `(R_xlen_t) REAL(x)[0]` |\n      238 +| 21 | `src/library/graphics/src/plot.c` | 115 | `(int) REAL(pch)[i]` |\n      239 +| 22 | `src/library/graphics/src/plot.c` | 208 | `(int) REAL(font)[i]` |\n      240 +| 23 | `src/library/graphics/src/par-common.c` | 315,317,320 | `(int)(REAL(value)[2])` |\n      241 +| 24 | `src/library/graphics/src/par-common.c` | 352,354,357 | `(int)(REAL(value)[2])` |\n      242 +| 25 | `src/library/grid/src/grid.c` | 5051 | `(int) REAL(pch)[i]` |\n      243 +| 26 | `src/library/grDevices/src/colors.c` | 1492 | `(int) REAL(x)[i]` |\n      244 +| 27 | `src/library/methods/src/methods_list_dispatch.c` | 344 | `(int) REAL(object)[0]` |\n      245 +| 28 | `src/main/subscript.c` | 140,261 | `(R_xlen_t) dblind` (safe) |\n      246 +| 29 | `src/main/seq.c` | 984-989,1024,1044 | `(int)(rfrom + ...)` (safe) |\n      247 +| 30 | `src/main/grep.c` | 114 | `(int)(xdouble*1024*1024)` (safe) |"
